      "On native macOS ARM64 sign the final executable with codesign --force --sign -, inspect its arm64 Mach-O architecture, and run codesign --verify --strict --verbose=2. Create the deterministic archive from those signed bytes, extract it to a temporary directory, then verify the extracted executable's signature and run its --version. Compute the manifest digest only after signing and archive assembly; no Developer ID/notarization claim.",
      "For x86_64-unknown-linux-musl and aarch64-unknown-linux-musl, inspect the executable extracted from each final archive using readelf headers for respectively Advanced Micro Devices X86-64 and AArch64, reject a PT_INTERP entry or DT_NEEDED dynamic dependencies, and run the extracted callisto --version on a native runner of the matching architecture. Require the expected coordinated product version and exit zero for both archives; a cross-compile alone is insufficient.",
